ctive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.6 stable\n- Not reproducible in Godot 4.5.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie) 13 on Wayland - Vulkan (Forward+)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn some bones configurations, for example there are 4 or more sibling bones with their own child from what I tested, some bones (1 in 2 or 1 in 4) will completely stop responding to the animation player after being moved manually. This persist even when reloading the scene and attempting to play an animation again. See video and reproduction project.\nThis doesn't happen in Godot 4.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee reproduction project.\nRotate the \"2\" bones, play animation \"test\", play animation \"RESET\", and bone \"D2\" will stop animating. Also note that bone \"B2\" rotates 180° instead of 90° as instructed in the \"test\" animation.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0107d437-6854-4010-8018-dae647197162\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bone-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25110253/bone-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab